### Physical review options

When a return needs you to physically inspect the returned (or cancelled) product's condition, the
return object includes a `physical_review_options` list. Each element represents one condition you
can report for this return's line items — use it to present the available options and to know what
is expected when you submit them to the [physical review endpoint](#submit-a-physical-review). For
where `physical_review_options` sits in the full response, see the
[return object](#return-object-attributes-appendix).

<%= render_code '{
  "physical_review_options": {
    "review_items": [
      { "option": "good", "comment_required": false },
      {
        "option": "damaged_product",
        "comment_required": true,
        "product_images_required": true,
        "packaging_images_required": true,
        "at_fault_option_required": true
      },
      {
        "option": "damaged_packaging",
        "comment_required": true,
        "product_images_required": true,
        "packaging_images_required": true,
        "at_fault_option_required": true
      },
      {
        "option": "wrong_product_returned",
        "comment_required": true,
        "product_images_required": false,
        "at_fault_option_required": true
      },
      {
        "option": "partially_damaged_product",
        "comment_required": true,
        "product_images_required": true,
        "packaging_images_required": true,
        "at_fault_option_required": true
      },
      {
        "option": "return_not_received",
        "comment_required": false,
        "at_fault_option_required": true
      },
      {
        "option": "return_received_incomplete",
        "comment_required": true,
        "product_images_required": true,
        "packaging_images_required": true,
        "at_fault_option_required": true
      }
    ]
  }
}', 'javascript' %>

Option | Meaning
------ | -------
`good` | the product (and its packaging) arrived back in good condition
`damaged_product` | the product itself is damaged
`damaged_packaging` | the packaging is damaged (the product itself may be fine)
`wrong_product_returned` | the customer sent back a different product than the one they ordered
`partially_damaged_product` | the product is only partially damaged
`return_not_received` | the item never actually arrived back at you
`return_received_incomplete` | fewer units were returned than the customer claimed
`delayed_return` | the return shipment arrived later than expected
`item_sent` | you're reporting that the item was in fact sent to the customer
`product_misclassified` | the product's Skroutz catalog listing was itself misclassified

`delayed_return`, `item_sent` and `product_misclassified` only ever appear in place of the standard
set above, for the specific line items they apply to — never alongside it.

#### Option fields

Each entry in `physical_review_options.review_items` has the following fields:

Field | Type | Description
----- | ---- | -----------
`option` | String | the condition to submit back to the [physical review endpoint](#submit-a-physical-review) for one or more line items
`comment_required` | Boolean | `true` if a non-blank `comment` must be submitted for a line item using this option, `false` if optional
`product_images_required` | Boolean | `true` if at least one product photo must be submitted for a line item using this option. Omitted entirely on options that never offer a product photo upload at all (`good`, `return_not_received`)
`packaging_images_required` | Boolean | `true` if at least one packaging photo must be submitted for a line item using this option. Omitted entirely on options that never offer a packaging photo upload at all (`good`, `return_not_received`, `wrong_product_returned`)
`at_fault_option_required` | Boolean | present, and only ever `true`, on every option except `good` — an `at_fault` value must be submitted for a line item using this option

### Submit a physical review

Report the condition of this return's line items by submitting, for each one, an `option` from
that return's current [`physical_review_options`](#physical-review-options).

**Prerequisites:**

* The return must currently be eligible for a physical review (see
  [Physical review options](#physical-review-options))
* Each submitted `reason` must be one of the `option` values currently listed in the return's
  `physical_review_options`

<pre class="terminal">
  POST /merchants/ecommerce/returns/:return_code/physical_review
</pre>

#### Request body

Request body | Type | Description
------------ | ---- | -----------
`review_items` | Array | One entry per line item being reported — see below
`return_reason_dispute` | Object | (Optional) — see [Disputing the return reason](#disputing-the-return-reason)

Unlike the merchants panel (which always submits every line item on the return, defaulting
unselected ones to `good`), this endpoint only records a decision for the line items you actually
include in `review_items` — include every line item you want a decision recorded for, even ones in
good condition.

Each element of `review_items`:

Field | Type | Description
----- | ---- | -----------
`line_item_id` | String | ID of the line item being reported (the same `id` value from [return line items](#return-line-items))
`reason` | String | (Optional) One of the `option` values from this return's `physical_review_options`. Omit it, or send `good`, to report the item as being in good condition
`quantity` | Integer | (Optional) How many units to report under this `reason`. Defaults to the line item's full remaining eligible quantity when omitted
`comment` | String | Required when the chosen option's `comment_required` is `true`
`at_fault` | String | `customer` or `courier`. Required when the chosen option's `at_fault_option_required` is `true`
`product_images` | Array of Files | Product photos, sent as `multipart/form-data` (up to 5 files, PNG/JPG/JPEG, 7MB per file). Required when the chosen option's `product_images_required` is `true`
`packaging_images` | Array of Files | Packaging photos, same constraints as `product_images`. Required when the chosen option's `packaging_images_required` is `true`

#### Disputing the return reason

For a limited subset of returns, you may optionally dispute the return reason the customer
selected, in addition to reporting the items' condition — the same question the merchants panel
asks as *"Is the return reason that the user selected correct?"*. Agreeing with it (or omitting
`return_reason_dispute` entirely) requires nothing further. Disputing it excludes this return from
your operational statistics.

Field | Type | Description
----- | ---- | -----------
`accepted` | Boolean | `true` if the customer's return reason is correct — no dispute is recorded, and `reason`/`comment` are ignored. `false` to dispute it
`reason` | String | Required when `accepted` is `false`. One of `withdrawal`, `wrong_size`, `content_mistake`, `damaged_courier_fault`
`comment` | String | Required when `accepted` is `false` — free-text explanation of why you disagree with the customer's reason

#### Example: reporting a damaged product

<pre class="terminal">
curl -X POST https://<%= settings.api_domain %>/merchants/ecommerce/returns/R-111111-1111111/physical_review \
  -H 'Accept: application/vnd.<%= settings.site_name %>+json; version=3.0' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer your_access_token_here' \
  -F 'review_items[0][line_item_id]=gY6oNzr8jp' \
  -F 'review_items[0][reason]=damaged_product' \
  -F 'review_items[0][at_fault]=courier' \
  -F 'review_items[0][comment]=Arrived with a cracked screen' \
  -F 'review_items[0][quantity]=1' \
  -F 'review_items[0][product_images][]=@product_photo.jpg' \
  -F 'review_items[0][packaging_images][]=@packaging_photo.jpg'
</pre>

#### Success Response

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "success": true
}', 'javascript' %>

#### Error Responses

**Return not found** (same as [retrieving a single return](#error-handling)):

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
</pre>

**Return not eligible for a physical review:**

<pre class="terminal">
HTTP/1.1 422 Unprocessable Entity
</pre>

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "return_status",
      "messages": [
        "The order is not eligible for physical review because of its current state."
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

The message varies with why the return isn't eligible right now — e.g. an ongoing service
inspection, an undelivered return shipment, or an existing pending physical review for the same
return.

**A required field is missing for a line item** (one `code`/`messages` entry per missing field,
indexed by the item's position in `review_items`):

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "review_items[0].comment",
      "messages": ["is required"]
    },
    {
      "code": "review_items[0].at_fault",
      "messages": ["is required"]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

`code` is one of `review_items[N].comment`, `review_items[N].quantity`, `review_items[N].at_fault`,
`review_items[N].product_images` or `review_items[N].packaging_images`, following the requirements
listed in [Option fields](#option-fields) for that item's chosen `reason`.

**Missing return reason dispute fields** (only when `return_reason_dispute.accepted` is `false`):

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "return_reason_dispute.reason",
      "messages": ["is required"]
    },
    {
      "code": "return_reason_dispute.comment",
      "messages": ["is required"]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

## Error handling

In case of errors, the response will have a representative HTTP status code
in the `4xx` range. The body would contain an array of `errors`.

For example, if the requested return code does not exist (or does not belong to your shop),
you will get a `404` HTTP status code (Not Found):

<%= render_code '{
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "not_found",
      "messages": [
        "Return not found"
      ]
    }
  ]
}', 'javascript' %>

